## 2. Production must hold

### 2.1 Last-ref free (ARC)

NORTHSTAR 1.2: Automatic Reference Counting with deterministic reclaim when the last reference drops.
ROADMAP: `PURE_NO_ARC=0`. Memory is freed when the last reference drops.
Official rebuild exports `PURE_NO_ARC=0`. The strip helper is only for `PURE_NO_ARC=1`.

Disk:
  `OoStrHeader` and `OoListHeader` hold `ref_count` (`chs_rt.h`).
  `oo_str_release` decrements. Count 0 calls `free` (`chs_rt_str.c`).
  List last-ref is atomic. Count 1 to 0 subtracts ambient bytes and frees (`chs_rt_list.c`).
  C emit prints `oo_*_release` on scope exit (`oodac/c_emit_arc.oo`).
  Interned literals set `OO_FLAG_STATIC`. Retain and release are no-ops by design (`chs_rt_str_intern.c`).

Status: done. Production requirement? yes. Open row? no.

Honesty note: `scripts/arc_smoke.oo` only checks that the fixture dir exists. It does not run the six fixtures. That is a thin lock, not a pin lie. Do not add a 5.3 LLVM row. Do not add a CLI/ops row this cycle.

### 2.2 Fail-closed zero quotas

SHIPPED: POSIX `setrlimit` is product under `&SysCap` (AS / NOFILE / CPU). Zero quotas fail closed.

Disk:
  `chs_rt_rlimit.c` rejects `megabytes <= 0`, `max_fds <= 0`, and `seconds <= 0` before `setrlimit`.
  `std/sec/rlimit.oo` repeats the same refuse.
  Fixture `fixtures/open_rlimit.oo` proves mem 0 and nofile 0 fail closed, then sets nofile 256.
  Lock: `scripts/open_rlimit_smoke.oo` (emit-c + gcc + run prints `open_rlimit: PASSED`).

Status: done. Production requirement? yes. Open row? no.

### 2.3 Ambient list quota

Default list budget is 64 MiB (`chs_rt_list.c`). `OO_LIST_AMBIENT_QUOTA` may raise it.
Over-budget list growth prints an error and exits. This is process-local. It is not OS rlimit.
`oo_alloc_bytes` is a smoke size token. It raises the ceiling. It does not `mmap` (`chs_rt_alloc.c`).
SECURITY.oot already names this as smoke quota tokens.

Status: done for the listed contract. Open row? no.

## 3. Product on disk, not 1.2 production leftover

### 3.1 Bump arenas

SHIPPED: `arena_create` / `alloc` / `reset` under AllocCap. `&ArenaCap` is its own token.
Disk: `chs_rt_arena.c`. Eight slots. Size 64 to 1<<28. Forged cap exits. Reset is O(1).
Proof: `fixtures/open84_arena_cap.oo` (OPEN-84 closed).
There is no `arena_destroy`. Slots stay live. That is a bound, not a 5.2 hole.

Status: done. Open row? no.

### 3.2 Checkpoint words

`oo_checkpoint` / `oo_rollback` store up to eight `long long` values (`chs_rt_arena.c`).
Proof: `fixtures/open86_checkpoint.oo` (OPEN-86 closed).
This is not undo-RAM.

Status: smoke. Open row? no.

## 4. NORTHSTAR 1.2 later (not this-cycle open)

### 4.1 Pause-free GC horizon

NORTHSTAR 1.2 names the horizon. NORTHSTAR 6.1 says later.
No collector symbol in `chs_rt_*.c`. ARC last-ref is the product path.
MOONSHOTS names Undo-RAM and ghost-state TM. Keep those rows there.

Status: residual / moonshot. Open row? no.

### 4.2 Zero-copy slices

NORTHSTAR 1.2 names zero-copy slicing across buffer boundaries.
Disk: `oo_str_slice` and `oo_byte_slice` allocate a new payload and `memcpy` (`chs_rt_str.c`).
Comments say not a borrow. SHIPPED does not claim zero-copy slices.

Status: residual. Open row? no.

### 4.3 Ghost-state transactional memory

NORTHSTAR 1.2 names speculative buffers with rollback before commit.
Disk is the eight-int stack in §3.2. Not a RAM undo log. Not isolated actor heaps.
Actors share the process heap (`chs_rt_actor.c`). Isolated heaps stay later.

Status: residual / moonshot. Open row? no.

